:: The Crack 2 [event main_quest] {"position":"5575,500","size":"100,100"}
/* Quest "The Access Log" (main_crackLogs), STAGE1_PROPOSAL.md 4.10, the Monday after The Crack. $ethan.name is completely
   normal. Then the server's access log: every raw log the company has ever recorded was pulled on Saturday night, from the
   login of $darius.name. I confront him. I'm wrong: he spent the weekend out of town, and he can prove it. He's hurt and polite
   about it. If I brought him in at Morale ($flags.dariusBroughtIn) he forgives fast; if I shut him out, it hits harder, and his
   morale with it. Who really pulled the logs is never said; I ask $ethan.name to reset everybody's passwords. */
<<silent>><<SetBackground $locations[14].img>><</silent>>
On Monday $ethan.name is the first one in, which never happens. He's brought donuts. He makes a joke about the elevator, and another one about $brian.name's new haircut, and he laughs at his own jokes the way he always does, too loud, slapping the desk. By ten he's arguing with $brian.name about emitter timings at exactly the usual volume.

Whatever I saw through the glass on Saturday, it's gone. He's fine. I decide that he's fine.

Then I open the server dashboard to check the overnight backups, and there's a line in the access log I don't recognize.

<<linkreplace "Read it">>
Saturday, 21:43. A full export of the raw sensor archive. Every reading from every unit we have ever run: the diner pilot, $boss.callName's office, the gyms, the Veil tests. The office vent, from the first day. All of it, packed into one file and downloaded in four minutes.

Next to it, the account that did it: $darius.name's.

I sit and look at that for a long time.

<<if $flags.dariusBroughtIn === true>>He has access to the raw data now. I gave it to him myself, the curated version of it, the week of the morale numbers. But he would never need to pull the whole archive at night, on a Saturday, in one go, unless he wanted all of it at once, without anyone watching, and the archive has things in it that I never cleaned.<<else>>He doesn't have access to the raw archive. I shut him out. And now his name is on a full export, on a Saturday night, when nobody was here. He kept the printout from that afternoon. He folded it and put it in his jacket instead of the bin.<</if>>

<<linkreplace "Call him over">>
<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $player, text: "$darius.name. Meeting room." },
{ text: "He looks up, sees my face, and closes his laptop without saving whatever he was working on, which I have never seen him do." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

<<silently>><<SetBackground $locations[15].img>><</silently>>
I turn the screen so he can see the log and don't say anything. He reads it standing up. I watch him read it twice.

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $darius, text: "That's my account." },
{ who: $player, text: "It is." },
{ who: $darius, text: "Saturday at 21:43." },
{ who: $player, text: "Where were you on Saturday at 21:43?" },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

<<linkreplace "Wait for his answer">>
He doesn't get defensive. That's almost worse. He takes out his phone, scrolls for a moment, and puts it on the table in front of me.

It's a photo. A crowded dining room, a long table, a lot of people in nice clothes, a cake with a big gold 40 on it. $darius.name is in the middle of it in a dark suit, with his arm around a woman who has his cheekbones.

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $darius, text: "My cousin's fortieth. In my parents' town, three hours north. I drove up Saturday morning and came back Sunday night. The timestamp is 21:38. That's me making a toast." },
{ who: $darius, text: "I can show you the toast too, if you want. It's not very good. I don't do toasts." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

I look at the photo, and the timestamp, and his face, which is perfectly calm and has gone a shade paler than usual.

He's telling the truth. He'd be a fool to lie about something this easy to check, and he isn't a fool. Somebody used his login. Somebody who knew his password, or found it, or didn't need it.

<<if $flags.dariusBroughtIn === true>>
<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $player, text: "I had to ask." },
{ who: $darius, text: "I know you did." },
{ text: "He picks his phone back up and puts it in his pocket. He doesn't look away from me while he does it." },
{ who: $darius, text: "I'd have asked too. In your position. It looks bad. It looks exactly like what it would look like if I'd done it." },
{ who: $darius, text: "But you brought me in, a few weeks ago. You told me the truth when you didn't have to. I'm not going to throw that away by stealing a file I could have asked you for." },
{ who: $player, text: "I'm sorry." },
{ who: $darius, text: "Accepted. Now, can we find out who actually did it? Because somebody in this office has my password, and I'd really like to know how." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

He's hurt. He's careful not to show it, and that's how I can tell. But he's on my side of the table, already thinking about the problem instead of about me. I brought him in, and today that bought me a lot.

<<run State.variables.darius.stats.morale = Math.clamp(State.variables.darius.stats.morale - 5, State.variables.darius.stats.min.morale, State.variables.darius.stats.max.morale)>>
<<else>>
<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $player, text: "I had to ask." },
{ who: $darius, text: "Of course." },
{ text: "He picks his phone back up and slides it into his pocket, very precisely." },
{ who: $darius, text: "May I go back to my desk? I have the gym report due at noon." },
{ who: $player, text: "$darius.name. I'm sorry." },
{ who: $darius, text: "There's no need. You were protecting your company. I understand completely." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

He means every word, and every word is a closed door. He walks back to his desk, opens his laptop, and works through lunch without speaking to anyone. When $sister.callName brings him his coffee, he thanks her the same way he thanks the vending machine.

I shut him out once, and today I accused him. In his notebook those are two data points, and he's very good at drawing lines between data points.

<<run State.variables.darius.stats.morale = Math.clamp(State.variables.darius.stats.morale - 20, State.variables.darius.stats.min.morale, State.variables.darius.stats.max.morale)>>
<<UpdateStat "-" "Morale" 3>>
<</if>>

<<linkreplace "Deal with it">>
<<silently>><<SetBackground $locations[14].img>><</silently>>
Back at my desk I look at the log line again for a while. Saturday, 21:43. A Saturday when the office should have been empty.

I don't let the thought go any further than that. I'm good at that. I've been good at it all weekend.

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $player, text: "$ethan.name. I need everybody's passwords reset today. New ones, long ones, two-factor on the server. Somebody's been sloppy." },
{ who: $ethan, text: "On it, boss. I'll make them so long nobody can remember them, including you." },
{ text: "He gives me a thumbs up over his monitor without looking away from his screen, and starts typing." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

<<UpdateStat "+" "Corruption" 1>>
<<NextQuest $player>>
<<ReturnFromEvent>>
<</linkreplace>>
<</linkreplace>>
<</linkreplace>>
<</linkreplace>>
